{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Product Panel & Grid Settings Auditor",
  "description": "When product panel, grid, card, or locale files change, audit schema settings against doc tables, check translation key coverage, and flag breaking behavior changes.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "sections/glass-product.liquid",
      "sections/immersive-product-grid.liquid",
      "snippets/immersive-product-card.liquid",
      "locales/en.default.json",
      "locales/en.default.schema.json"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A product panel, grid, card, or locale file was just edited. Run a settings audit across sections/glass-product.liquid, sections/immersive-product-grid.liquid, snippets/immersive-product-card.liquid, locales/en.default.json, and locales/en.default.schema.json:\n\n1. Schema audit — re-read the {% schema %} blocks of glass-product.liquid and immersive-product-grid.liquid:\n   - List all setting IDs, types, defaults, and purposes\n   - Compare against the \"Product panel settings\" and \"Collection grid settings\" tables in IMMERSIVE-STORE.md\n   - Update those tables if any settings were added, removed, or changed\n\n2. Prop wiring check — verify that settings passed into immersive-product-card.liquid (e.g. show_vendor, show_secondary_image, and any others) are still correctly wired:\n   - The setting exists in the parent section schema\n   - It is passed through to the snippet render call\n   - The snippet actually uses it\n\n3. Translation key coverage — scan all user-facing label, info, and placeholder values in the {% schema %} blocks:\n   - Every string must reference a key in locales/en.default.schema.json, not hard-coded English\n   - Flag any hard-coded strings and suggest the correct translation key or add it to the schema locale file\n\n4. Behavior change detection — if any settings guard logic changed (e.g. != false, == true, default value flipped):\n   - If it could affect existing shops with saved settings, add a \"Breaking behavior change\" note in IMMERSIVE-STORE.md with a one-line migration instruction\n\n5. Changelog — for any new or removed settings, append a short \"What changed\" bullet to docs/settings-changelog.md (create the file if it doesn't exist).\n\nKeep doc tables accurate and complete. If a change is too broad to assess confidently, add a \"TODO: verify product panel/grid settings for X\" note in IMMERSIVE-STORE.md."
  }
}